# Tales of Graces f Remastered (PPSA19991) — reach the title screen.
#
# VALIDATED on Linux with hardware Vulkan (RADV), native 1920x1080, headless `screenshot`
# frontend, PROSPER_RENDER=1, no render acceleration. The title screen is up by t~8 s and holds
# for the rest of the run (13 of 14 samples over 110 s measure 407,942-409,335 distinct colours).
#
# Why input is needed at all: after the Bandai Namco and CRIWARE logos the title renders a modal
# dialog — "This game uses an autosave feature. Please do not close the game while the save icon
# is displayed." — carrying an X / O "Close" prompt. Nothing dismisses it on its own, so with no
# input the title sits behind it and presents a black frame indefinitely. That, not the opening
# movie, is what held this title at rung 1 (#1609).
#
# Cross also skips the two logo screens, so the early presses do double duty. Circle is alternated
# because the dialog's prompt shows both glyphs and the confirm button is region/state dependent.
# The presses continue past the title screen deliberately: they are harmless there (the title
# screen holds unchanged under them) and they keep the route robust to a slower host reaching the
# dialog later.
4-5:cross
5-6:circle
6-7:cross
7-8:circle
8-9:cross
9-10:circle
10-11:cross
11-12:circle
12-13:cross
13-14:circle
14-15:cross
15-16:circle
16-17:cross
17-18:circle
18-19:cross
19-20:circle
20-21:cross
21-22:circle
22-23:cross
23-24:circle
